          "The Extended Family: Encompasses multiple generations: parents, children, grandparents, uncles, aunts, nephews, nieces, and in-laws. Advantages: Communal child-rearing ('it takes a village to raise a child'), strong safety net during bereavement or illness, rich cultural socialization. Disadvantages: Heavy financial dependency burden on successful individuals, frequent family disputes over inheritance.",
